T:The Old Tap Dance
% NFF Book 2006
S:from the playing of the Brown boys & Daryl Maynard & Steve Lowery & Laurie Lowery, Cape Barren Island, Tas
S:recording held by Tas Aboriginal Council, Hobart
H:From the playing of Les Brown, An Aboriginal fiddler from Tasmania. Recorded in the 1960's. The Brown Boys band played an eclectic mix of old time, trad and country around Tasmania for years. This tune has been found in other districts as well. We don't know where it comes from. They played it for their Uncle Alfie or Affie wanted to tap dance.  Greg O'Leary, September 2024
N:A version of this tune was collected from Harry McQueen, Castlemaine, Vic
N:who knew it as "McGlashan's Step Clog"
B:Fred Pribac & Stuart Graham, 'Tasmanian Dance Tunes', Cygnet Folk Festival, 2000
O:Australia, Tas, Cape Barron Island
